# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your actual values.
# Never commit .env.local itself.

# Google Air Quality API — powers the live air-quality dimension.
# Google Cloud console → enable "Air Quality API" → create an API key.
# Restrict the key to that one API; it is called server-side only, so it
# does NOT need to be NEXT_PUBLIC and must not be.
#
# Why this one: it is modelled on a 500m grid rather than tied to physical
# monitoring stations, so every coordinate returns a value — no coverage
# gaps, and a new city needs zero data work for this dimension. India's
# default index is ind_cpcb, so the number is the real Indian CPCB AQI on
# its native 0–500 scale rather than a converted foreign one.
#
# Cost: 10,000 requests/month free, then USD 5 per 1,000. /api/aqi caches
# for 24h, so ~268 pins ≈ 8,040 calls/month — inside the free tier. Do not
# shorten that cache without doing the arithmetic first.
#
# Optional. Without it the air dimension falls back to the stored reading
# in data/aslivastu/master_by_pin.json and the methodology table shows
# STORED instead of LIVE — everything still renders. Note that 27 pins
# (Gurugram, Noida, Ghaziabad, Faridabad — the NCR satellite cities) have
# NO stored reading, so without this key those areas are scored on 7 of
# 8 dimensions, with air's weight redistributed to the other seven.
GOOGLE_AIR_QUALITY_KEY=

# Supabase → Project Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# Google AI Studio (aistudio.google.com/apikey) — powers the SunScout
# "AI Report" button (Gemini Vision shadow analysis) AND the floor-plan
# furnishing advisor (/floor-plan-analysis, Gemini Vision floor-plan
# reading). Without this, the rest of the site works fine but both of
# those features return a 500.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
